Z||000000||Frank R||04-15-2000||01:37 PM||||Greetings..I have copied info by Paul Vargas on this subject, but alas the RPO list does not include all numbers from my '86 SE.  Here are the options. A31  BC8  BW1  BX1  B34  C49  DG7  D34  D7W  E52  e52  e9y n82  pon  vj7  vf5  6ja  7ja  8xd  84p  9xd ...  This car has 62 options listed.  Ca. car...22K miles<BR>Has wood steering wheel.....Frank R||||reg||6
Z||000001||Old Lar||04-15-2000||02:51 PM||||I pulled out my Fiero Spotter's Guide by Mark Corbin.  Vin # 1G2P F(SE) 37 R(for 4 cyl) 9(for V6) G (for 86) P******.<P>1G2PF379GP****** would be the vin # for an SE<P>The Fiero Option Production numbers that are listed are: Total Production for 1986: 83974<P>AD3/SUNROOF........50,230 MADE<BR>AF9 LUMBAR SEAT  N/A<BR>AU3/POWER LOCKS.....36,383<BR>A01/TINT GLASS......63,392<BR>A31/POWER WINDOWS...35,294<BR>A90/ DECK RELEASE<BR>BC8/ DOOR POCKETS<BR>B34/ MATS, CARPET<BR>CD4/INTER WIPERS....62,729<BR>CJB/T-TOP        N/A<BR>C49/DEFOG...........28,197<BR>C60/AC..............74,989<BR>DG7/POWER MIRROR....18,225<BR>D34/ VANITY MIRROR<BR>D42/ENGINE COMPARTMENT SCREEN (1984)<BR>D80/SPOILER DECK LID (1985-8)<BR>K05/ENGINE BLOCK HEATER (1984-7)<BR>K34/CRUISE..........44,069<BR>LR8/4CYLINDER.......38,040<BR>L44/V-6.............45,934<BR>MM4/4SPD............17,856<BR>MM5/5SPD............24,013<BR>MX1/AUTO............42,105<BR>NB2/ CALIF EMISSIONS<BR>NK3/FORMULA STEERING WHEEL 3 SPOKE(1984-5)<BR>NP4 LEATHER WRAPPED 4 SPOKE (1986-7)<BR>NP5 LEATHER WRAPPED THREE SPOKE(1985-5)<BR>N24 WHEELS TURBO FINNED<BR>N33/TILT WHEEL<BR>N41 POWER STEERING <BR>N78/WHEELS HI TECH TURBO COLOR COORDINATED (1986-7)<BR>PB4/ WHEEL LOCKING PACKAGE<BR>PX1/ SAME AS N24<BR>PO2 WHEEL COVERS<BR>PO6/ WHEEL  TRIM RINGS<BR>TR9/ LAMP GROUP<BR>UA1/HEAVY DUTY BATTERY<BR>VK3 FRONT LICENCE PLATE BRACKET<BR>VO8/ COOLING HEAVY DUTY<BR>V53 LUGGAGE CARRIER DELETE<BR>V56 LUGGAGE CARRIER DECK LID<BR>V58 SAME AS V56<BR>WS6/PERFORMANCE PACKAGE (1984-5)<BR>WS9/HIGH MILAGE COUPE (1985-6)<BR>WV9/VALUE LEADER COUPE<BR>W02 SPORT APPEARENCE PACKAGE(1988)<BR>W66/ FORMULA OPTION<BR>Y82 INDY PACE CAR<BR>Y99 RALLY TUNED SUSPENSIOM (1985-6)<BR>Z49 EXPORT ( CANADA)<P>STYLED WHEELS.......58,614<BR>CLOTH SEATS.........81,148<BR>LEATHER SEATS........2,855<BR>AM RADIO..............872<BR>AM/FM RADIO.........19,121<BR>" WITH CASSETTE.....39,291<BR>" " WITH EQUILIZER..23,551<BR>DIGITAL CLOCK.......81,963<P>These are all the codes listed.  I never saw a stock Fiero with a wood steering wheel.  Remember that a lot of parts can be easily interchanged on a Fiero, so chances are you may have had some dealer installed options at some time or replacement parts from other cars including the wheel tub where the list of codes are pasted to.<P><BR>D42 AND N41 WERE NEVER BUILT FOR PUBLIC AVALABILITY.<P>There is more inf in Mark's guide.<P>FIERO SPOTTER'S GUIDE<BR>5474 S.R. 19             <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Galion, OH 44833<P>Make check payable to Mark Corbin<p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 04-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||04-15-2000||06:43 PM||||and here is the ones you missed<BR>BW1-ornamentation,exterior, rear end<BR>BX1- ornamentation,exterior,front end (special)<BR>D7W speedo gear driven<BR>E5Z speedo gears less adapter<BR>E9Y vehicle speed sensor<BR>PON pontiac assembly plant<BR>84P wheel color grey<BR>the 6xx 7xx 8xx 9xx are the spring codes.<BR>||||reg||1
